---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Show, SignInButton, SignUpButton } from '@clerk/astro/components';
import {
	URL_ACCOUNT_USER,
	getSiteUrlConfig,
	hostedMcpOrigin,
	resolveHostedMcpRpcUrl,
} from '../lib/site-urls';

const cfg = getSiteUrlConfig(import.meta.env);
const { urlStandard, urlMcpMarketing, urlMcpEndpoint } = cfg;

const claudeMcpRpcUrl = resolveHostedMcpRpcUrl(urlMcpEndpoint || 'https://mcp.aadm.io');
const claudeMcpOriginOnly = hostedMcpOrigin(claudeMcpRpcUrl);

const claudeMcpFullConfigSnippet = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "aadm": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "${claudeMcpRpcUrl}",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "<your token here>"
      }
    }
  }
}`;
---

<Layout
	title="AADM + Claude Code — MCP setup and workflows"
	description="Connect Claude Desktop and Claude Code CLI to the hosted AADM MCP: subscriber token, HTTP transport, Navigator / Investigator / Sentinel workflows, and illustrative deep-dive transcripts."
	headerActiveNav={null}
>
	<main id="main">
		<!-- Hero -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-12 pt-16 sm:px-6 sm:pb-16 sm:pt-24">
			<p class="mb-4 inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">
				<span class="rounded-full border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/60 px-3 py-1 text-orange-300/95">
					AADM + Claude Code
				</span>
				<span class="rounded-full border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/60 px-3 py-1 text-accent-violet">
					MCP · Streamable HTTP
				</span>
			</p>
			<h1 class="font-display max-w-4xl text-4xl font-extrabold leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
				Standard in the cloud.
				<span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-300 via-amber-200 to-accent-violet bg-clip-text text-transparent">
					Claude Code in your repo.
				</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
				Point Claude Desktop or Claude Code at the hosted AADM MCP the same way you wire any HTTP MCP: subscriber token,
				stable tools for briefs and doctrine, and your codebase still owns proof—tests, CI, and traces.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
				<a
					href="#connect-claude"
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-600 via-orange-600 to-violet-600 px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-orange-950/30 transition hover:brightness-110"
				>
					Connection steps & copy-paste
				</a>
				<a
					href={urlMcpMarketing}
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition hover:border-slate-500/40 hover:bg-surface-mid"
				>
					MCP overview & pricing
				</a>
				<a
					href={urlStandard}
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-slate-600 px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-slate-300 transition hover:border-slate-500 hover:text-white"
				>
					Read the standard
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Connect (below fold) -->
		<section
			id="connect-claude"
			class="scroll-mt-24 border-y border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/45 py-14 sm:scroll-mt-28 sm:py-16"
			aria-labelledby="connect-claude-heading"
		>
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
				<h2 id="connect-claude-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
					Connect AADM MCP to Claude
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
					One subscriber token, one HTTP MCP endpoint. Replace{' '}
					<code class="font-mono-cta text-emerald-300/90">&lt;your token here&gt;</code> with the key from your AADM
					dashboard (often <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">ak_…</code>). Do not commit real secrets.
				</p>

				<div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-12">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-300/90">Steps</h3>
						<ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-300">
							<li>
								<Show when="signed-out">
									<span>
										<SignUpButton
											mode="modal"
											class="inline font-semibold text-accent-violet underline decoration-accent-violet/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-blue"
										>
											Sign up
										</SignUpButton>
										{' '}
										or{' '}
										<SignInButton
											mode="modal"
											class="inline font-semibold text-accent-violet underline decoration-accent-violet/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-blue"
										>
											sign in
										</SignInButton>
										on <a href={urlMcpMarketing} class="text-accent-violet underline hover:text-accent-blue">aadm.io/mcp</a>,
										subscribe, then open{' '}
										<a href={URL_ACCOUNT_USER} class="text-accent-violet underline hover:text-accent-blue">your account</a>{' '}
										to mint an MCP-capable API key.
									</span>
								</Show>
								<Show when="signed-in">
									<span>
										<a href={URL_ACCOUNT_USER} class="font-semibold text-accent-violet underline hover:text-accent-blue">
											Open your account
										</a>{' '}
										and mint or copy an MCP API key (
										<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">ak_…</code>).
									</span>
								</Show>
							</li>
							<li>
								Merge the JSON below into your Claude config’s <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">mcpServers</code>{' '}
								object (see paths for Desktop vs Claude Code).
							</li>
							<li>
								Use the raw token in <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">Authorization</code>, or{' '}
								<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">Bearer ak_…</code> if your build expects that prefix.
							</li>
							<li>
								Fully quit and reopen <strong class="text-slate-200">Claude Desktop</strong>, or start a{' '}
								<strong class="text-slate-200">new Claude Code</strong> session in the terminal after saving—hosts do not
								always hot-reload MCP definitions.
							</li>
							<li>
								In chat, ask Claude to use AADM tools (e.g. <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">standard_brief</code>,{' '}
								<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">debug_defect</code>,{' '}
								<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">fetch_auth</code>). Confirm{' '}
								<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">tools/list</code> shows <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">aadm</code>.
							</li>
						</ol>

						<div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/70 p-5">
							<h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Where to paste</h4>
							<dl class="mt-3 space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-400">
								<div>
									<dt class="font-semibold text-orange-200/90">Claude Desktop</dt>
									<dd class="mt-1 font-mono-cta text-xs text-slate-500">
										macOS: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
									</dd>
									<dd class="mt-1 font-mono-cta text-xs text-slate-500">
										Windows: %APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json
									</dd>
									<dd class="mt-1 font-mono-cta text-xs text-slate-500">
										Linux: ~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
									</dd>
								</div>
								<div>
									<dt class="font-semibold text-orange-200/90">Claude Code (CLI / IDE extension)</dt>
									<dd class="mt-1">
										User scope: <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">~/.claude.json</code> — merge{' '}
										<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">mcpServers</code>. Optional project file:{' '}
										<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">.mcp.json</code> in the repo root for teams that version a
										shared template (still keep secrets out of git).
									</dd>
								</div>
							</dl>
							<p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
								Anthropic’s filenames and reload rules can change by release—double-check current Claude docs if something
								does not register. You can also try <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-600">claude mcp --help</code> on recent
								CLI builds for add/import flows.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="min-w-0">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
							<p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">
								<code class="font-mono-cta normal-case text-slate-400">mcpServers.aadm</code> — copy ready
							</p>
							<button
								type="button"
								id="claude-connect-copy-btn"
								class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-orange-500/45 bg-orange-700/90 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-md transition hover:bg-orange-600 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-orange-400 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-[#0c0d14]"
							>
								Copy JSON
							</button>
						</div>
						<pre
							class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-[#0a0d14] p-4 font-mono-cta text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-300 shadow-inner sm:text-sm"
							id="claude-connect-config-pre"
							role="region"
							aria-label="Example Claude MCP configuration JSON"
						><code id="claude-connect-config-code">{claudeMcpFullConfigSnippet}</code></pre>
						<p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">
							RPC URL: <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">{claudeMcpRpcUrl}</code>
							<span class="text-slate-600"> · </span>
							Discovery origin: <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-400">{claudeMcpOriginOnly}/</code>
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<script is:inline>
			(function () {
				const btn = document.getElementById('claude-connect-copy-btn');
				const code = document.getElementById('claude-connect-config-code');
				if (!btn || !code) return;
				const defaultLabel = btn.textContent || 'Copy JSON';
				btn.addEventListener('click', async function () {
					const text = (code.textContent || '').trim();
					try {
						await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
						btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
						btn.classList.add('opacity-90');
						window.setTimeout(function () {
							btn.textContent = defaultLabel;
							btn.classList.remove('opacity-90');
						}, 2200);
					} catch {
						btn.textContent = 'Copy blocked — select text';
						window.setTimeout(function () {
							btn.textContent = defaultLabel;
						}, 3200);
					}
				});
			})();
		</script>

		<!-- Desktop vs terminal -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="claude-modes-heading">
			<h2 id="claude-modes-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
				Claude Desktop vs Claude Code in the terminal
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
				Both can attach to the same HTTP MCP. The difference is where your files and shell session live—not what AADM
				ships over the wire.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
				<article class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/85 p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20">
					<h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-orange-200">Claude Desktop</h3>
					<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
						GUI app, broad integrations, good for docs-centric sessions and walking stakeholders through{' '}
						<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">standard_brief</code> outputs. Paste logs and HAR excerpts into chat;
						pair with local repos manually when you need file paths.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/85 p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20">
					<h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-accent-violet">Claude Code (terminal)</h3>
					<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
						Runs against a working tree: read, search, diff, test commands, and multi-step refactors in one thread.
						Ideal for Investigator loops—MCP supplies gates and doctrine; the CLI supplies{' '}
						<strong class="text-slate-300">evidence</strong> from your machine.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- What Claude can do -->
		<section class="border-y border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/35 py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="claude-can-heading">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
				<h2 id="claude-can-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
					What Claude Code can do with AADM MCP
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
					The MCP does not edit your repo. Claude Code does. Together they keep turns structured: orchestrator metadata,
					AUTH text on demand, and troubleshooting rails that resist premature fixes.
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-accent-violet">Navigator-style delivery</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							Pull <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">plan_delivery</code>, doctrine slices, and AUTH cites while
							shaping a feature across layers.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-accent-blue">Investigator defects</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							Use <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">debug_defect</code> for gated recon and classification; append
							evidence across turns without rewriting the brief from scratch.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-violet-200">Sentinel assurance</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							Run <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">audit_run</code> / <code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">audit_outline</code>{' '}
							for seam language; bind horizontal boundaries while Claude traces files locally.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-orange-200">AUTH literacy</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">fetch_auth</code> returns the real markdown for{' '}
							<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">AUTH-XX</code> so reviews cite governance text—not memory.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-200">Orchestrator hooks</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">route_lane</code>,{' '}
							<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">orchestrator_anchor</code>, and{' '}
							<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">standard_brief</code> give deterministic branching for long sessions.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/75 p-5">
						<h3 class="font-semibold text-emerald-300/90">Proof stays local</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
							MCP never replaces CI. Claude runs tests you invoke; pass/fail remains authoritative in your pipeline.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Fictional deep dive -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="claude-session-heading">
			<h2 id="claude-session-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
				Illustrative session: ~2h seam hunt (Claude Code + AADM MCP)
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
				Fictional transcript—timestamps show how MCP calls and local investigation interleave during a horizontal seam
				bug (gateway ↔ worker ↔ idempotency). Not captured from a live recording.
			</p>

			<figure
				class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[#3a3530] bg-[#14120f] shadow-2xl shadow-black/45 ring-1 ring-orange-950/30"
				aria-label="Fictional Claude Code terminal session with MCP tool calls"
			>
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-[#2d2926] bg-[#1c1917] px-3 py-2">
					<div class="flex gap-1.5 pl-1" aria-hidden="true">
						<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#ff5f57]/90"></span>
						<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#febc2e]/90"></span>
						<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#28c840]/90"></span>
					</div>
					<span class="flex-1 text-center font-mono-cta text-[11px] text-slate-500">payments-worker · claude · zsh</span>
					<span class="w-14 shrink-0"></span>
				</div>

				<div class="max-h-[min(720px,70vh)] overflow-y-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono-cta text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
					<p class="text-orange-300/85">[09:14]</p>
					<p class="mt-1 text-slate-500">
						<span class="text-slate-400">you</span> — Duplicate charges after retries. Gateway logs show 202 + worker shows single consume.
						Suspect seam between API idempotency key and queue dedupe. Wired AADM MCP—want Investigator framing + AUTH cites for
						idempotency + jobs.
					</p>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[09:16]</p>
					<p class="mt-1 text-slate-400">
						<span class="text-violet-300">claude</span> — I’ll take a structured lane first, then we’ll anchor evidence before touching code.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-violet-500/35 bg-[#1a1625]">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-violet-500/25 bg-violet-950/35 px-3 py-1.5">
							<span class="rounded bg-violet-600 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
							<code class="text-emerald-300">route_lane</code>
							<span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500">intent: defect</span>
						</div>
						<pre class="p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-500">{`→ routing_basis: EXPLICIT_WORKFLOW_INTENT
→ primary_tool: debug_defect
→ recommended_next_tools: [ "debug_defect", "fetch_auth", "standard_brief" ]`}</pre>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[09:21]</p>
					<div class="mt-1 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-sky-500/25 bg-[#0f1724]">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-sky-500/20 bg-sky-950/30 px-3 py-1.5">
							<span class="rounded bg-sky-700 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
							<code class="text-sky-300">fetch_auth</code>
							<span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500">AUTH-25 · AUTH-28</span>
						</div>
						<p class="p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-500">
							→ Loaded markdown for duplicate/idempotent handling themes (illustrative)—we’ll map claims to gateway vs worker
							code paths next.
						</p>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[09:35]</p>
					<div class="mt-1 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-amber-500/35 bg-[#1c1410]">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-950/25 px-3 py-1.5">
							<span class="rounded bg-amber-700 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
							<code class="text-amber-200">debug_defect</code>
							<span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500">Path A · UNCLASSIFIED</span>
						</div>
						<pre class="p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-400">{`WHAT THIS MEANS · Single next action:
Run one replay: POST /pay with same Idempotency-Key + body hash,
capture gateway response headers AND worker dequeue span id.

Forbidden right now: patch mapper + broaden retries in same turn.`}</pre>
					</div>
					<p class="mt-2 text-slate-500">
						<span class="text-violet-300">claude</span> — Running curl replay against staging with your{' '}
						<code class="text-slate-600">.env.staging</code> headers…
					</p>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[10:02]</p>
					<p class="mt-1 text-slate-500">
						<span class="text-slate-400">you</span> — Pasted HAR row + worker trace: dequeue twice same payload id, gateway still returned cached 202 body from first attempt.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-amber-500/35 bg-[#1c1410]">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-950/25 px-3 py-1.5">
							<span class="rounded bg-amber-700 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
							<code class="text-amber-200">debug_defect</code>
							<span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500">append_evidence</span>
						</div>
						<p class="p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-500">
							→ Still UNCLASSIFIED until we tie duplicate dequeue to idempotency scope (per-key vs per-route vs worker lease).
						</p>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[10:48]</p>
					<p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">
						<span class="text-violet-300">claude</span> — Grepped repo: idempotency middleware stores key in Redis with TTL; worker consumer builds dedupe key from message body only—omits tenant id when queue fan-out expands.
					</p>

					<p class="mt-6 text-orange-300/85">[11:30]</p>
					<div class="mt-1 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-[#0f1a17]">
						<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-950/30 px-3 py-1.5">
